    "result_text": "The build succeeds. The full suite has only the acceptance test (the others are base classes). The change is complete and green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented email-uniqueness rejection on owner creation in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (the sole `POST /api/owners` handler; the v2 controller only lists owners).\n\n**Changes to `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:**\n\n1. Added a conflict check in `addOwner`, alongside the existing telephone-in-use check:\n   ```java\n   if (isEmailInUse(owner.getEmail())) {\n       return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.CONFLICT);\n   }\n   ```\n\n2. Added an `isEmailInUse` helper (mirroring the existing `isTelephoneInUse`) that lower-cases both the candidate and each stored email and returns true on any match. A null/empty candidate email is never in use, so email-less owners (the default `ownerNode()` payload used throughout the tests) don't collide.\n\nThe comparison is case-insensitive; the `Owner` model's `setEmail` already lower-cases stored values, and the helper lower-cases defensively on both sides.\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
